      "source": "Quizlet",
      "question": "Dell Computer makes its suppliers wait 37 days on average to be paid for their goods; however, Dell is paid by its customers immediately. If Dell can earn an annual interest rate of 4%, what is this float worth to Dell per dollar spent on inputs?",
      "answer": "Dell earns interest on this float, the money that they implicitly borrow without paying interest on it. 37/365 = 1/10 of a year. So in addition to the 4% interest rate, they also earn 1/10(4%) = 0.4%. Hence, for every million paid to its suppliers, it saves 0.004(1000000)= 4000 dollars.",
